### Pruebas manuales desde Visual Studio
### Las llaves se leen de tus user-secrets (ver http-client.env.json); nunca se escriben aquí.
### Arriba a la derecha del editor elige el ambiente "dev".

@host = http://localhost:5034

### 1) Salud de la API y de la BD (no pide llave)
GET {{host}}/health

### 2) Rutas de salida de Blaster (comprueba la API key de Voices)
GET {{host}}/api/blaster/outbound-routes
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 3) Simular el webhook de Voices (llamada contestada)
POST {{host}}/webhooks/blaster/call-result
Content-Type: application/json
X-Webhook-Secret: {{webhookSecret}}

{
  "message_id": "prueba-001",
  "status": "SENT",
  "operator": "telcel",
  "is_mobile": true,
  "outbound_route": "90135",
  "phone_number": "5544332211",
  "sip_code": 200,
  "sip_description": "OK",
  "call_type": "initial",
  "duration_minutes": 0,
  "duration_seconds": 42
}


### 4) Consultar la llamada guardada
GET {{host}}/api/blaster/calls/prueba-001
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 5) Salud con detalle (BD + bandeja: pendientes / rechazados)
GET {{host}}/health/detalle

### 6) Estado de la bandeja de avisos
GET {{host}}/api/blaster/inbox
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 7) Simular webhook SMS "Message status"
POST {{host}}/webhooks/sms/message-status
Content-Type: application/json
X-Webhook-Secret: {{webhookSecret}}

{
  "message_id": "prueba-sms-001",
  "status": "SENT",
  "datetime": "2026-11-04T16:00:01.000Z"
}

### 8) Simular webhook SMS "Batch status" (lote)
POST {{host}}/webhooks/sms/message-status
Content-Type: application/json
X-Webhook-Secret: {{webhookSecret}}

{
  "type": "BATCH",
  "batch_id": "prueba-lote-001",
  "status": "COMPLETED",
  "datetime": "2026-11-04T16:05:00Z",
  "total": 2,
  "messages": [
    { "message_id": "prueba-sms-001", "status": "SENT", "datetime": "2026-11-04T16:00:01Z" },
    { "message_id": "prueba-sms-002", "status": "FAILED", "datetime": "2026-11-04T16:00:03Z" }
  ]
}
